{"reasoning": "The user is asking a multi-hop question: 'Who is the president of the new country that jointly established a Commission of Truth and Friendship with the country that broadcasts Dahsyat?'.\n\nStep 1: Identify the 'country that broadcasts Dahsyat'. Passage 5 states that 'Dahsyat (or Strikes, also stylized as dahSyat) is an Indonesian television show broadcast daily on Rajawali Citra Televisi Indonesia (RCTI).' Therefore, the country broadcasting Dahsyat is Indonesia.\n\nStep 2: Identify the 'new country' that jointly established a Commission of Truth and Friendship with Indonesia. Passage 7 describes the 'Indonesia–Timor Leste Commission on Truth and Friendship', which was 'established jointly by the governments of Indonesia and East Timor in August 2005'. Thus, the new country is East Timor (Democratic Republic of Timor-Leste).\n\nStep 3: Identify the president of that new country (East Timor). Passage 1 states that Xanana Gusmão was elected as the country's first president. The document details several presidents over time.\n\nThe question asks for 'the president of the new country'. Since the establishment date of the commission is August 2005, and East Timor became independent in May 2002 (Passage 1), the presidency during or immediately after this period needs to be determined. Xanana Gusmão was elected as the first president in March 2002.\n\nThe available information lists presidents: Xanana Gusmão (first president, elected 2002), José Ramos-Horta (elected later), Francisco Guterres (elected May 2017), and Taur Matan Ruak/José Ramos-Horta (later).\n\nSince the commission was established in August 2005, Xanana Gusmão was president at that time. He is mentioned as the 'country's first president'. Given the phrasing 'the new country', this likely refers to the sovereign state of East Timor.", "finding": "The country broadcasting Dahsyat is Indonesia (Passage 5). The commission established jointly with Indonesia is the Indonesia–Timor Leste Commission on Truth and Friendship, established by Indonesia and East Timor in August 2005 (Passage 7). Xanana Gusmão was elected as East Timor's first president in March 2002 (Passage 1), making him the president of 'the new country' (East Timor) during the commission's establishment date.", "answer": "Xanana Gusmão", "next_query": null}
