{"reasoning": "The original question is: \"What is the seat of the county sharing a border with the county in which J. P. Hayes was born?\"\n\nThis requires several steps:\n1. Determine the county where J. P. Hayes was born.\n2. Identify counties that share a border with that county.\n3. Find the 'seat' (county seat) of one of those bordering counties.\n\nStep 1: Locate J.P. Hayes's birthplace from Passage 6. Passage 6 states: \"Hayes was born and raised in Appleton, Wisconsin.\"\n2. Determine the county for Appleton, Wisconsin. While not explicitly stated in Passage 6 regarding his birth, Passage 7 (Pulaski High School) mentions that Pulaski HS serves parts of Shawano, Outagamie, and Oconto counties. Passage 8 (John C. Petersen) states he was from \"Appleton, Wisconsin\" and served as a member of the Wisconsin State Assembly from **Outagamie County**.\nSince J.P. Hayes was born in Appleton, WI, it is highly likely that his county is Outagamie County, given the context provided by other documents mentioning Appleton residents associated with specific counties (Passage 8).\n\nStep 2: Identify counties bordering Outagamie County, Wisconsin.\nNo document explicitly lists the border counties of Outagamie County. I need to search for this geographical information.", "finding": "J. P. Hayes was born in Appleton, Wisconsin. John C. Petersen (also from Appleton) served from Outagamie County. Therefore, we assume J.P. Hayes was born in Outagamie County.\nPulaski High School serves parts of Brown, Shawano, Outagamie, and Oconto counties.", "answer": null, "next_query": "counties bordering Outagamie County Wisconsin"}
